BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.573 0.251 0.055 rg 54.00 215.00 Td (MATHEMATICAL FORMULATION: HAVERSINE DISTANCE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.471 0.208 0.059 rg 54.00 198.00 Td (The great-circle geodesic distance d between successive coordinates \(phi1, lambda1\) and \(phi2, lambda2\) is computed as:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.5 Tf 0.118 0.161 0.231 rg 72.00 180.00 Td (a = sin^2\(d_phi / 2\) + cos\(phi1\) * cos\(phi2\) * sin^2\(d_lambda / 2\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.5 Tf 0.118 0.161 0.231 rg 72.00 165.00 Td (d = 2 * R_earth * atan2\(sqrt\(a\), sqrt\(1 - a\)\)      [where R_earth = 6,371,000 m]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.471 0.208 0.059 rg 54.00 148.00 Td (Vectorized in pipeline/preprocessing.py using NumPy arrays, achieving processing speeds exceeding 150,000 pings/sec.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.471 0.208 0.059 rg 54.00 134.00 Td (Instantaneous velocity between sequential pings is calculated as v = d / delta_t.) Tj ET
