BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.200 0.255 0.333 rg 56.00 730.00 Td (Public buses regularly stop at designated bus shelters to pick up and drop off passengers, often idling for 30 to 120 seconds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.200 0.255 0.333 rg 56.00 716.00 Td (During dwell time, the GPS continues broadcasting: lat/lon remain stationary, while velocity drops to 0.0 - 2.5 km/h.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.863 0.149 0.149 rg 56.00 702.00 Td (If naively averaged into road segment traffic, these stationary buses falsely register arterial roads \(like Ring Road\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.863 0.149 0.149 rg 56.00 688.00 Td (as 'Severe Gridlock', when traffic is actually flowing at 45 km/h. Filtering out dwell time is mission-critical.) Tj ET
